{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/Se","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/SE","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/SQ","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/SH"],"type":"inheritsFrom"},{"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherited By","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyle"],"type":"inheritedBy"},{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Date\/HTTPFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Date\/ISO8601FormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DateComponents\/HTTPFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DateComponents\/ISO8601FormatStyle"],"type":"conformingTypes"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FormatStyle","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"FormatInput","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials11FormatStyleP0C5InputQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/FormatInput"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FormatOutput","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials11FormatStyleP0C6OutputQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/FormatOutput"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Decodable","preciseIdentifier":"s:Se","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encodable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SE","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Types conforming to the "},{"code":"FormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol take their input type and produce formatted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instances of their output type. The formatting process accounts for locale-specific conventions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like grouping and separators for numbers, and presentation of units for measurements. The format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"styles Foundation provides produce their output as "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"AttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instances. You"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can also create custom styles that format their output as any type, like XML or JSON "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an image."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There are two basic approaches to using a "},{"code":"FormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create an instance of a type that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" and apply it to one or more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instances of the input type, by calling the style’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/format(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Use this when you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"want to customize a style once and apply it repeatedly to many instances."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass an instance of a type that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" to the data type’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method, which takes the style as a parameter. Use this for one-off formatting scenarios, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when you want to apply different format styles to the same data value. For the simplest cases,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most types that support formatting also have a no-argument "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted()"},{"type":"text","text":" method that applies a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"locale-appropriate default format style."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Foundation provides format styles for integers ("},{"code":"IntegerFormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), floating-point numbers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"FloatingPointFormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), decimals ("},{"code":"Decimal.FormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), measurements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"Measurement.FormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), arrays ("},{"code":"ListFormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and more. The numeric format styles"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also provide supporting format styles to format currency and percent values, like"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"IntegerFormatStyle.Currency","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Decimal.FormatStyle.Percent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Modifying-a-format-style","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Modifying a format style"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Format styles include modifier methods that return a new format style with an adjusted behavior."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The following example creates an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IntegerFormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":", then applies modifiers to round values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"down to the nearest 1,000 and applies formatting appropriate to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fr_FR"},{"type":"text","text":" locale:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let style = IntegerFormatStyle<Int>()","    .rounded(rule: .down, increment: 1000)","    .locale(Locale(identifier: \"fr_FR\"))","let rounded = 123456789.formatted(style) \/\/ \"123 456 000\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Foundation caches identical instances of a customized format style, so you don’t need to pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format style instances around unrelated parts of your app’s source code."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Accessing-static-instances","level":3,"text":"Accessing static instances"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Types that conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" typically extend the base protocol with type properties or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type methods to provide convenience instances. These are available for use in a data type’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method when the format style’s input type matches the data type. For example,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the various numeric format styles define "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number"},{"type":"text","text":" properties with generic constraints to match"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the different numeric types ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Float16"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To see how this works, consider this example of a default formatter for an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Because"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"123456789"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryInteger"},{"type":"text","text":", its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method accepts an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IntegerFormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameter. The following example shows the style’s default behavior in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en_US"},{"type":"text","text":" locale."}]},{"code":["let formatted = 123456789.formatted(IntegerFormatStyle()) \/\/ \"123,456,789\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IntegerFormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" extends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" with multiple type properties called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number"},{"type":"text","text":", each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of which is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IntegerFormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" instance; these properties differ by which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryInteger"},{"type":"text","text":"-conforming type they take as input. Since one of these statically-defined"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties takes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" as its input, you can use this type property instead of instantiating a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new format style instance. Using dot notation to access this property on the inferred"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" makes the call point much easier to read, as seen here:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let formatted = 123456789.formatted(.number) \/\/ \"123,456,789\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Furthermore, since you can customize these statically-accessed format style instances, you can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rewrite the example from the previous section without instantiating a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IntegerFormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like this:"}]},{"code":["let rounded = 123456789.formatted(.number","    .rounded(rule: .down, increment: 1000)","    .locale(Locale(identifier: \"fr_FR\"))) \/\/ \"123 456 000\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Parsing-with-a-format-style","level":3,"text":"Parsing with a format style"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To perform the opposite conversion — from formatted output type to input data type — some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format styles provide a corresponding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParseStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":" type. These format styles typically expose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an instance of this type as a variable, called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parseStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParseStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":" one of two ways:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Initialize the data type by calling an initializer of that type that takes a formatted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance and a parse strategy as parameters. For example, you can create a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decimal"},{"text":" from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"formatted string with the initializer ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decimal.init(_:format:lenient:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a parse strategy and call its "},{"code":"parse(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method on one or more formatted instances."}]}]}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Performing-formatting","title":"Performing formatting","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/format(_:)"]},{"anchor":"Setting-style-locale","title":"Setting style locale","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/locale(_:)"]},{"anchor":"Declaring-input-and-output-types","title":"Declaring input and output types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/FormatInput","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/FormatOutput"]},{"anchor":"Applying-date-and-time-styles","title":"Applying date and time styles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/iso8601-1jmw1","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/iso8601-2hxhp","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/http-26iub","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/http-3z94y"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials"]]},"metadata":{"platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"15.0"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"1